// nvmidi_ui_keys.nvgt - one helper the examples put in front of ui_pump: did
// the user just ask to stop?
//
// The split from nvmidi_ui.nvgt is not cosmetic. ui_pump is the loop's own
// heartbeat, and the examples call it once per frame; this is the question
// asked once per key read. Keep them apart and a script can keep pumping the
// window while it ignores the exit key.
//
// Escape is written the same way here as in the first version of
// list_ports.nvgt, where it was measured to work: a plain key_pressed read.
// key_held combines the two spellings the engine actually has - key_pressed is
// true while the key is down, key_repeating adds the auto repeat - because
// their names are all this repository could observe from the engine, and it is
// their effect that has to hold on both a stuck alt and an ordinary press.
bool a_key(const int k) {
	return key_pressed(k) || key_repeating(k);
}

bool stop_key() {
	if (key_pressed(KEY_ESCAPE)) return true;
	return (keyboard_modifiers & KEYMOD_ALT) > 0 && a_key(KEY_F4);
}

// No entry point here, and that is measured rather than an omission. The five
// examples include this file and define their own main(); an included file's
// main() is not a declaration, so adding one here gave every one of them
// "A function with the same name and parameters already exists" (run
// 37012913997). A file that is only ever included does not need one.
